#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063984 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2b47545-fdf1-5e6a-b0bb-bbbecb8067cc" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Positive Integer Exponent"}] :question/id #uuid "eff323d1-4e70-5490-8e41-9fbf00c387f5" :question/math-academy-id "e-446" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int (3x+1)^3 \\, \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nu=3x+1\n$$\n\nThen differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = 3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = \\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm d u\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u$, calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int(3x + 1)^{3}dx &= \\intu^{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\intu^{3}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{u^{4}}{4} + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{12}u^{4} + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{12}(3x + 1)^{4} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}[\\frac{1}{12}(3x + 1)^{4} + C] &= \\frac{1}{12} \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}[(3x + 1)^{4}] + \\frac{d}{dx}(C) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{12} \\cdot 4(3x + 1)^{3} \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(3x + 1) + 0 \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}(3x + 1)^{3} \\cdot 3 \\\\\n&= (3x + 1)^{3}✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063985 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "387d85df-b839-5837-89b9-5e4bb4daa073" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Negative Integer Exponent"}] :question/id #uuid "e469c042-9619-55d4-b745-d4ed26251d80" :question/math-academy-id "e-447" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int \\dfrac{2}{(1-x)^3} \\, \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int 2(1-x)^{-3} \\, \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nLet $u=1-x$. Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -1\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = -\\textrm d u\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u$, calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int2(1 - x)^{-3}dx &= \\int2u^{-3} \\cdot (-1)du \\\\\n&=-2\\intu^{-3}du \\\\\n&=-2 \\cdot \\frac{u^{-2}}{-2} + C \\\\\n&= u^{-2} + C \\\\\n&= (1 - x)^{-2} + C \\\\\n&= (1)/((1 - x)^{2}) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}[(1)/((1 - x)^{2}) + C] &= \\frac{d}{dx}[(1)/((1 - x)^{2})] + \\frac{d}{dx}(C) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dx}[(1 - x)^{-2}] + \\frac{d}{dx}(C) \\\\\n&=-2(1 - x)^{-3} \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(1 - x) + 0 \\\\\n&= - (2)/((1 - x)^{3}) \\cdot (-1) \\\\\n&= (2)/((1 - x)^{3})✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063988 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ae5760b-9277-596c-8546-dca4fd985bd7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Fractional Exponent"}] :question/id #uuid "e416cb5c-22df-55e4-a3cb-c6b5dfc650c3" :question/math-academy-id "e-448" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle\\int\\sqrt{1-5x}\\,\\textrm d x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the integral as\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int(1-5x)^{1/2}\\,\\textrm d x\n$$\n\nNow, we let $u=1-5x$. Then differentiating with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -5\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = -\\dfrac 1 5 \\textrm d u\n$$\n\nWe now write our integral in terms of $u$, calculate the integral as normal, and write the final answer in terms of $x$ at the very end:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int(1 - 5x)^{1/2}dx &= \\intu^{1/2} \\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5})du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{5}\\intu^{1/2}du \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{5} \\cdot \\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2} + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{15}u^{3/2} + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{15}(1 - 5x)^{3/2} + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(1 - 5x)^{3}} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's double-check that our result is correct. If we differentiate the result, then it should come out to the original integrand:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}[- \\frac{2}{15}\\sqrt{(1 - 5x)^{3}} + C] &= -\\frac{2}{15} \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}[\\sqrt{(1 - 5x)^{3}}] + \\frac{d}{dx}(C) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{15} \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}[(1 - 5x)^{3/2}] + \\frac{d}{dx}(C) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{2}{15} \\cdot \\frac{3}{2}(1 - 5x)^{1/2} \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(1 - 5x) + 0 \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{5}(1 - 5x)^{1/2} \\cdot (-5) \\\\\n&= (1 - 5x)^{1/2}✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064777 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ae5760b-9277-596c-8546-dca4fd985bd7" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating an Algebraic Function With Fractional Exponent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8be0f720-9b24-5463-8644-62fdf3a5fc13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{4y - 1}}{4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063173} {:answer/id #uuid "97aade93-135e-551c-a502-cbfd409ab108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{4y - 1} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063174} {:answer/id #uuid "ad134924-29f6-57ac-861c-e86a6ac5d741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{4y - 1}}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063175} {:answer/id #uuid "c94b14ad-ec68-5f9f-9a09-be0bc0cc4024" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{4y - 1}}{3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063176} {:answer/id #uuid "f68959d6-0379-5187-ba8a-5695f9810a85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{4y - 1}}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063177}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad134924-29f6-57ac-861c-e86a6ac5d741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{4y - 1}}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063175} :answer-field/id #uuid "85340826-8abf-586a-8f9f-3e28f87917d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063172}] :question/id #uuid "6c4056b3-c70d-593e-9370-73ee76b66f6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-49391" :question/problem "What is $\\displaystyle \\int\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4y - 1}}dy$?"}]}
